# Gable frontend — example environment configuration
#
# Copy this file to `.env` (or `.env.local`) in the `app/` directory and adjust
# as needed:
#
#     cp .env.example .env
#
# Vite only exposes variables prefixed with `VITE_` to the browser bundle
# (via `import.meta.env`). Everything in this file is NON-SECRET, public
# configuration that is safe to commit as an example and safe to ship in a
# client build. Never put API keys, database URLs, or JWT secrets here — those
# are backend concerns (see backend configuration and `.do/` deploy specs).

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# VITE_API_URL — base URL the SPA prefixes onto every `/api/...` request.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Leave EMPTY for local development and for any deployment where the frontend
# and backend share one origin (the dev server and the production nginx/App
# Platform routing both forward `/api/*` to the backend on the same host).
#
#   - Local dev (Vite proxy handles /api):     VITE_API_URL=
#   - Same-origin deploy (recommended):        VITE_API_URL=
#   - Separate backend origin:                 VITE_API_URL=https://api.example.com
VITE_API_URL=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# VITE_DEMO_MODE — mount the local "surface picker" landing page at `/`.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# When "true", `/` renders a dev launcher for choosing which UI surface (ERP,
# portal, yard, driver, POS) to exercise, instead of the ERP dashboard. Handy
# for public demo builds. Leave unset/false for a normal deployment.
# VITE_DEMO_MODE=false

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# VITE_API_PROXY — dev server only. Target the Vite dev proxy forwards `/api`
# to (see app/vite.config.ts). Defaults to http://localhost:8080 when unset.
# Not used in production builds. Set this if your backend runs on another host
# or port during local development.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# VITE_API_PROXY=http://localhost:8080
